Subject: Remove the warnings post-0073 code introduced

What this does
  Removes variables, functions and macros that post-0073 code left unused:
  three `old1` locals read only under `#if !QJS_DRC` (hoisted into that
  branch), an unused `imm`, an unused `it`/`nx` pair per iterator-close handler
  (the decoding load stays), `np`/`ns`/`np2`/`ns2` in four liveness loops,
  `k` in two fuse passes, `shift`, `opcode`/`nr_buf`/`var_refs`, `enc_ok`,
  `encode_reg_count`, `deferred`, `nreg`, `n_edges` and `atom_count`; the
  `regvm_t_get_field_chain_free1` and `js_scan_argv_safe` declarations that go
  with their already-guarded definitions.

Why we need it
  Each is a `-Wunused-variable`, `-Wunused-function` or
  `-Wunused-but-set-variable` warning in one or more configurations, and every
  one is dead storage or a stale store. Removing them shrinks the source and
  keeps the warning counts falling.

What it adds
  No new API. Runtime only.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

